# Kandelo patch rationale (S43)
# Judgment: Supported. Keep operation-mode propagation until the object
# design replaces it because callback failure policy depends on the actual
# operation rather than script strictness alone.
#
# Node property callbacks ask whether failure should throw before taking
# action. The answer depends on the operation: Reflect and Object.assign
# can differ even in the same script. Bridge-entry checks or script
# strictness miss operations performed entirely inside JS. Keep operation-
# mode propagation until a native-object redesign provides it faithfully;
# the OS cannot supply it. Nested user calls must not inherit the wrong
# caller's failure mode.
#
# Retained provisionally; see README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

Carry property-operation error policy into native callbacks.

Keep original property algorithms and ordering. Explicit JSAPI/Reflect modes
and native Throw=true operations override caller strictness; RunScript clears
the mode for reentrant user code. The context owns no JS edges here.

